              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a bank (of a pond or river), then the Bengali for to moor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: স্রোত",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্রোত — srot — \"a current; a stream\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "নদীর স্রোতে নৌকাটা দ্রুত চলল। nôdīr srote noukāṭā drutô chôllô. The boat moved fast on the river's current."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a flow of people or things: মানুষের স্রোত (srot), a stream of people."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "স্রোত (srot) is Sanskrit srotas, \"the current or bed of a river, a stream\" (Monier-Williams), from sru, to flow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
